# Server API conventions

## Controllers

- `[ApiController]`, role `[Authorize(Roles = AppRoles.X)]`, route `api/{role}/{resource}`.
- Primary-constructor inject `ISender` only when possible.
- Resolve user id from claims; return `Unauthorized()` if missing.
- Map with `result.ToActionResult()` (`ResultExtensions`).
- Add `[ProducesResponseType]` for success and common error shapes.

```csharp
[ApiController]
[Authorize(Roles = AppRoles.Teacher)]
[Route("api/teacher/lessons")]
public sealed class LessonsController(ISender sender) : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpGet]
    public async Task<IActionResult> GetMyLessons(CancellationToken ct)
    {
        var userId = GetUserId();
        if (userId is null) return Unauthorized();
        var result = await sender.Send(new GetMyLessonsQuery(userId.Value), ct);
        return result.ToActionResult();
    }
}
```

## Do not

- Put business logic or EF queries in controllers.
- Bypass MediatR for feature work.
- Hand-edit generated OpenAPI client; change the API and rebuild so NSwag runs.

## Realtime / cross-cutting

- Notifications push via SignalR (`NotificationsHub`, `/hubs/notifications`).
- Prefer `GlobalExceptionHandler` + ProblemDetails for unexpected errors.
- Language comes from `RequestLanguageMiddleware` — preserve that pipeline.
